        "original_id": "69cfc7a2-dbe8-5142-a15a-aba2ba4dc69c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Hodge, Danny Boyle, Irvine Welsh, Alex Garland\n- Works: Trainspotting, Shallow Grave, A Life Less Ordinary, The Beach, The Final Curtain, Alien Love Triangle\n- Topics: screenwriting, film adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- John Hodge, born in 1964, is a British screenwriter and dramatist.\n- John Hodge is most noted for adapting Irvine Welsh's novel Trainspotting into the screenplay for the film Trainspotting.\n- John Hodge's film credits include Shallow Grave (1994), Trainspotting (1996), A Life Less Ordinary (1997), The Beach (2000), The Final Curtain (2002), and the short film Alien Love Triangle (2002).\n- The Beach is a 2000 British-American adventure drama film directed by Danny Boyle.\n- The Beach is based on Alex Garland's 1996 novel of the same name.\n- John Hodge adapted Alex Garland's novel The Beach for the film The Beach.",
